   "mechanism": "Bias, a property of approximate balance; the standard error is in band. With delta = 0.02 the minimum-dispersion weights stop on the tolerance boundary, so each covariate keeps an imbalance of 0.02 standard deviations in the direction of the raw imbalance, and the estimate keeps that imbalance times the outcome slopes (about 0.02 to 0.03 here, a quarter to four tenths of a standard error at n = 1000). Where the row is also flagged for coverage, that bias is the reason: the interval has the right width and sits off centre. The bias is gone at delta = 0.001 (sbw.att.tight) and, for a fixed delta, grows relative to the standard error with n. Before this screen the standard error was 1.5 times too large and hid it (see before_fix). The docstring of delta now states the bias.",
